TESTSUITE "REGNAVG regional average calculator"

*> Every case reaches the CALL "LOGALERT" boundary (it's inside an IF, but
*> reachability is static, not data-flow -- unmocked would refuse
*> UNMOCKED_CALL even in cases whose data never trips the threshold).
BEFORE-EACH
    MOCK CALL "LOGALERT"
        MOVE "OK" TO WS-ALERT-STATUS
    END-MOCK
END-BEFORE

*> Subscripted MOVE/EXPECT targets, comma+space and no-space forms.
*> Region 1's exact-division average needs no ROUNDED behavior to read
*> correctly. This case's own PERFORM target (1000-CALCULATE-REGION-1-
*> AVERAGE) never touches region 2 at all, so region 2's average -- read
*> through both REDEFINES siblings -- is checked at its clean starting
*> value here.
TESTCASE "region 1 divides evenly and clears the alert threshold"
    MOVE 100.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1, 1)
    MOVE 100.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1 2)
    MOVE 100.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1,3)
    PERFORM 1000-CALCULATE-REGION-1-AVERAGE
    EXPECT WS-MONTH-AMT(1, 1) TO BE 100.00
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(1) TO BE 100.00
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG-DISPLAY(1) TO BE "0010000"
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG-NUMERIC(1) TO BE 10000
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(2) TO BE 0
    VERIFY CALL "LOGALERT" WAS CALLED ONCE

*> 50.00 + 50.00 + 51.10 = 151.10; /3 = 50.3666... -- ROUNDED must give
*> 50.37, not the truncated 50.36. This case PERFORMs
*> 2000-CALCULATE-REGION-2-AVERAGE only, which never recomputes region 1
*> -- so `EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(1) TO BE 0` is load-bearing proof that
*> reset actually ran between cases: the previous case left it at 100.00,
*> and nothing in THIS case's own execution path would overwrite that if
*> reset hadn't cleared it first.
TESTCASE "region 2 rounds up to 50.37, not truncated to 50.36"
    MOVE 50.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(2 1)
    MOVE 50.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(2,2)
    MOVE 51.10 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(2, 3)
    PERFORM 2000-CALCULATE-REGION-2-AVERAGE
    EXPECT WS-MONTH-AMT(2 3) TO BE 51.10
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(2) TO BE 50.37
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG-DISPLAY(2) TO BE "0005037"
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG-NUMERIC(2) TO BE 5037
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(1) TO BE 0
    VERIFY CALL "LOGALERT" WAS CALLED NEVER

*> Closes the loop, and this is the load-bearing REDEFINES-reset proof:
*> this case PERFORMs 1000-CALCULATE-REGION-1-AVERAGE only, which never
*> touches region 2. The previous case left WS-REGION-AVG(2) at 50.37 --
*> readable through both its REDEFINES siblings. If cross-case reset
*> didn't clear that group, these EXPECTs would see 50.37/"0005037"
*> leftover, not a fresh zero; nothing in this case's own execution path
*> would overwrite it either way.
TESTCASE "a third case's fresh region 1 data doesn't inherit an earlier case's region 2 average"
    MOVE 10.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1,1)
    MOVE 10.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1,2)
    MOVE 10.00 TO WS-MONTH-AMT(1,3)
    PERFORM 1000-CALCULATE-REGION-1-AVERAGE
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(1) TO BE 10.00
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG(2) TO BE 0
    EXPECT WS-REGION-AVG-DISPLAY(2) TO BE "0000000"
    VERIFY CALL "LOGALERT" WAS CALLED NEVER
